    "prompt": "Below is a description of the Python function `BaseModel.model_rebuild`.\n\nDescription:\n\"\"\"\nThe `model_rebuild` function is a class method in Pydantic's `BaseModel` that forces a rebuild of the model's schema. It exists to ensure that the model's schema is up-to-date, especially when the model's fields or configuration might have changed. The function accepts several parameters: `force` to force a rebuild regardless of the current state, `raise_errors` to control whether exceptions should be raised during the rebuild, `_parent_namespace_depth` to determine how far up the call stack to look for the namespace, and `_types_namespace` to provide a custom namespace for type resolution. It returns `None` if a rebuild is not needed, or a boolean indicating whether the rebuild was successful. The function relies on several helper functions and methods, including `_typing_extra.parent_frame_namespace` to get the namespace from a parent frame, `_model_construction.unpack_lenient_weakvaluedict` to unpack the parent namespace, `_namespace_utils.NsResolver` to resolve namespaces, and `_model_construction.complete_model_class` to perform the actual rebuild. If `raise_errors` is `True`, the function will raise exceptions if errors occur during the rebuild. The function has side effects, as it modifies the class by deleting the cached schema and potentially rebuilding it.\n\"\"\"\n\nSplit the description into atomic claims. Each claim must be a single, self-contained factual statement about the function that could be checked against the function's source code (name the function explicitly; no pronouns referring to other claims). Do not add claims that are not in the description; do not merge two facts into one claim. Keep the original wording where possible. Assign each claim exactly one type:\n- \"structural\": the function's signature, parameter names/defaults/types, return type, or which functions, methods, classes or attributes it uses.\n- \"dataflow\": how